## Purpose

Repair noetic-dev delivery governance after verified false equivalences between validators and tests, self-review and independent QA, and publication/checkpoint status.

## Scope

- machine-readable delivery vocabulary, state/authority transitions, model profiles, command registry, issue status, and evidence manifest;
- genuine governance tests under `tests/`, distinct from repository validators;
- fail-closed implementation-pass : QA-pass cardinality, stale-SHA, role-independence, WIP/stack, issue-closure, workflow-pinning, and publication gates;
- process-isolated Pi dispatch wrapper with explicit role/model/tool/run evidence;
- PR template and CI separation of validations, tests, QA, independent high-reasoning agent review, merge readiness, and post-merge publication;
- bootstrap honesty: local evidence is advisory; publication remains blocked until trusted runner provenance and an independent Fable or Sol review process are established.

## Acceptance

- implementation follows the passed external planning artifact and is produced by one distinct implementation agent;
- every implementation/remediation generation receives exactly one distinct read-only QA agent against an immutable candidate SHA;
- `python3 scripts/validate_repo.py` is reported only as validation;
- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` runs genuine positive and adversarial tests;
- negative fixtures reject validator-as-test, self-QA, missing/multiple/stale QA, mismatched SHA/base/probe/execution, locally forged attestation, unsupported model, WIP/draft, stacked PR, blocked closure, author/stale approval, mutable Actions refs, and branch-name publication;
- independent approval is delegated to an authorized Fable or Sol profile at high or stronger reasoning, remains distinct from implementation and QA identities, and is bound to the immutable current candidate SHA;
- no review, independence, evidence, validation, or process requirement is removed by delegation;
- no PR is opened while the existing ten-PR publication freeze remains in force;
- trusted-runner infrastructure and independent-agent review are not claimed until actually established and verified.

## Non-goals

No merge, deployment, feature implementation, mass PR rewrite, removal of review/process requirements, or weakening of protected `main`.

